{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1511569-how-to-write-this-up","id":1511569,"title":"How to write this up?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-13T15:34:57-07:00","id":1511569,"title":"How to write this up?","content":"The character is a person who got infected by a \u201cnanotech bug\u201d that took him apart a cell at a time, replacing each with a nanite equivalent. The result is that the victim gets turned into the equivalent of a T-1000, the \u201cliquid metal Terminator\u201d from T-2. <br /> <br /> If the process had been fully successful, the character's mind would have been replaced by a digital mind networked with the Deviant that infected him or her, resulting in being part of a hive mind; and I want the Conspiracy of Loyalists to consist of that hive mind. But something went wrong with the process, resulting in the character coming out of it isolated from the network, but also mentally wiped: if it has any memories at all, they're extremely spotty and unreliable \u2014 kind of like a Promethean's residual memories. That and some difficulty to feel or understand emotions are the Scars that I have in mind for the Renegade; a suppression of free will is the main Scar I'm thinking of for the Loyalists. <br /> <br /> How would you write this up, and what else might you do with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T17:44:39-07:00","id":1511573,"title":"","content":"So, to start with, I think Boneless 3 is good enough start for being a liquid person. I think that's is probably a persistent Variation. The other powers I remember from the movie was mimicking the clothes, body, and voices of others, and turning arms and stuff into blades. I think Arm to Blade is a melee cutting Lash, with however many dots, and the mimicking others is perfectly described as Face Thief 3, right down to the clothes. I guess it's full body nanomachines, so persistent Anomalous Biology is in order...unfortunately probably 4 or 5. Scars can be any combo of Amnesia, Frozen Heart, and Subliminal Conditioning/Alternate Persona for the loyalists. Alternate Persona might be good if not all of the Hive Mind made it out of the character, or maybe Glitch, Paranoia, or Hallucinations if it's only fragments of it remaining. Personally, I like Dependency on materials to repair and maintain your nanomachine body, so you might need to eat metal and plastic and stuff. I don't know, seems fun accidentally being caught eating a car for parts or something. Looks like you will need at least one scar at 4 or 5, but the rest can be a more manageable 3 or 4, since most of your stuff is at 3 dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-13-2023, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}